(844182, 93314, 11078, '<td valign="top">Hello  Johanna  from the Critique Club <br/> <br/>This is a very good image. Focus is excellent.<br/> <br/>(I was thinking of doing something like this myself but couldnt get anyone to sit for me.)<br/>Your model has a very lovely eye <br/>Although the light reflection in her eye is a bit over powering and stands out quite a bit <br/> <br/>Personally I can''t see a lot wrong with your image except In my opinion you could have focused on the eye alone and left the brow out it has good enough focus for that. A really nice Macro<br/> <br/> I think maybe the title is a little strange for a CD Album cover and the font used is not the greatest and that is what let you down<br/> <br/>There were a lot of very good images in this challenge <br/>Your score was very good and nothing to be ashamed of I think you met the challenge very nicely<br/>So enjoy your photography and Good luck in future challenges <br/>If you have any questions please feel free to PM me.<br/>Regards<br/>Sally</td>', 'Hello  Johanna  from the Critique Club  This is a very good image. Focus is excellent. (I was thinking of doing something like this myself but couldnt get anyone to sit for me.)Your model has a very lovely eye Although the light reflection in her eye is a bit over powering and stands out quite a bit  Personally I can''t see a lot wrong with your image except In my opinion you could have focused on the eye alone and left the brow out it has good enough focus for that. A really nice Macro  I think maybe the title is a little strange for a CD Album cover and the font used is not the greatest and that is what let you down There were a lot of very good images in this challenge Your score was very good and nothing to be ashamed of I think you met the challenge very nicelySo enjoy your photography and Good luck in future challenges If you have any questions please feel free to PM me.RegardsSally', '2004-08-05 06:12:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(844191, 92986, 11078, '<td valign="top">Hello Marac from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>This is a wierd sort of image. I like it very much yet it is quite spooky with that head sort of just hanging there (I am not going to look at it any more I have to go to bed soon! LOL!)<br/> <br/>The guitar does look super imposed how did you do that it almost looks one dimentional <br/>The detail, focus, lighting are great colour very good <br/> <br/>There were a lot of good images in this challenge and I think the voters seemed to be put off by fonts as I look through the comments of yours and others. I think your image did well but it is very frustrating when others seem to do much better<br/>Your idea may have put a few people off.  Spooky! The name is good for a rock C D <br/>I hope that you have sucess in future challenges and I wish you Good Luck<br/>If you have any questions please feel free to P M me <br/>Regards<br/>Sally</td>', 'Hello Marac from the Critique Club This is a wierd sort of image. I like it very much yet it is quite spooky with that head sort of just hanging there (I am not going to look at it any more I have to go to bed soon! LOL!) The guitar does look super imposed how did you do that it almost looks one dimentional The detail, focus, lighting are great colour very good  There were a lot of good images in this challenge and I think the voters seemed to be put off by fonts as I look through the comments of yours and others. I think your image did well but it is very frustrating when others seem to do much betterYour idea may have put a few people off.  Spooky! The name is good for a rock C D I hope that you have sucess in future challenges and I wish you Good LuckIf you have any questions please feel free to P M me RegardsSally', '2004-08-05 06:26:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(844204, 93567, 11078, '<td valign="top">Hello John from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>I havent a clue what the title stands for but I do like the style of words you used (The font) it looks like text on a rock album <br/> <br/>You have used too many objects with very different patterns and it makes me almost dizzy trying to look at it.<br/>I like the two faces you have in your image and I think it would have helped if you focused on them with a plain background and left the other items out.<br/>A plain background would also make your text stand out.<br/> <br/>It seems unfair to vote you so low when you have obviously tried the colour is good ,but please try to remember that simple is sometimes better and there were a whole lot of excellent images in this challenge, and D P C have a very high standard <br/>I hope that you will continue to enjoy your photography and have better luck in your future challenges <br/>If you have any questions please feel free to P M me <br/>Regards<br/>Sally</td>', 'Hello John from the Critique Club I havent a clue what the title stands for but I do like the style of words you used (The font) it looks like text on a rock album  You have used too many objects with very different patterns and it makes me almost dizzy trying to look at it.I like the two faces you have in your image and I think it would have helped if you focused on them with a plain background and left the other items out.A plain background would also make your text stand out. It seems unfair to vote you so low when you have obviously tried the colour is good ,but please try to remember that simple is sometimes better and there were a whole lot of excellent images in this challenge, and D P C have a very high standard I hope that you will continue to enjoy your photography and have better luck in your future challenges If you have any questions please feel free to P M me RegardsSally', '2004-08-05 06:40:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(844235, 92897, 11078, '<td valign="top">Hello Steve from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Well! what can I say. So near and yet so far. What a shame because the score is very high  This is an amazing image so beautiful and you have captured it so well. Beautiful lighting and focus.<br/>Your score is excellent and only just missed the ribbon <br/>For myself I would choose yours as a ribbon winner but I am only one vote and there can be only 3 ribbons <br/>Good title for a rock band <br/>Myself I am not keen on the style of font used but, hey, who really looks at the font when you have a great image but the voters comments say they like it with a few exceptions<br/>Its just a shame you missed out but that''s no reflection on your image<br/>Keep the good work coming our way and you will surely be a ribbon winner.<br/>Nice work Enjoy your photography Good luck in future challenges <br/>If you have any questions please feel free to PM me <br/>Regards<br/>Sally <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello Steve from the Critique Club Well! what can I say. So near and yet so far. What a shame because the score is very high  This is an amazing image so beautiful and you have captured it so well. Beautiful lighting and focus.Your score is excellent and only just missed the ribbon For myself I would choose yours as a ribbon winner but I am only one vote and there can be only 3 ribbons Good title for a rock band Myself I am not keen on the style of font used but, hey, who really looks at the font when you have a great image but the voters comments say they like it with a few exceptionsIts just a shame you missed out but that''s no reflection on your imageKeep the good work coming our way and you will surely be a ribbon winner.Nice work Enjoy your photography Good luck in future challenges If you have any questions please feel free to PM me RegardsSally  ', '2004-08-05 06:54:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(845707, 93011, 22734, '<td valign="top">from the critique club:<br/> <br/>  I somehow knew that it was going to be tough for this picture to end up high. Nothing to do with the quality. Simply, the subject matter. The edgy comps have an uphill fight in DPC. <br/>  But let us talk about this one. Here you managed the triangle and in a most interesting manner. All the black leave unfinished, giving that grand trine feel. In other words the triangle continues outside the confines of the physical visible area. You did wise with the type selection. It fits the character of the smart composition. I believe you did everything correct. Even the color is good and so are the kisses. The only minor change I would have made was to shift over the song name and space it from the edge the same distance you did with DPC. However to end up at 5.4 with this concept is a good negation to those that love to vote down this image.<br/> <br/>Personally I like this shot because it looks convincing and because it has a touch of humor. The composition is tight, the color is great and the general feel is "cool." I feel you did a very nice job and i feel it is complete.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-08-05 22:24:11.</i></td>', 'from the critique club:   I somehow knew that it was going to be tough for this picture to end up high. Nothing to do with the quality. Simply, the subject matter. The edgy comps have an uphill fight in DPC.   But let us talk about this one. Here you managed the triangle and in a most interesting manner. All the black leave unfinished, giving that grand trine feel. In other words the triangle continues outside the confines of the physical visible area. You did wise with the type selection. It fits the character of the smart composition. I believe you did everything correct. Even the color is good and so are the kisses. The only minor change I would have made was to shift over the song name and space it from the edge the same distance you did with DPC. However to end up at 5.4 with this concept is a good negation to those that love to vote down this image. Personally I like this shot because it looks convincing and because it has a touch of humor. The composition is tight, the color is great and the general feel is "cool." I feel you did a very nice job and i feel it is complete.', '2004-08-05 23:21:54.000000', '2004-08-05 23:24:11.000000', 0),
